     "explanation": "The order matters functionally, not as a willpower trick. Hyperfocus loads your mind with the facts, constraints, and half-formed ideas of a problem; scatterfocus then plays with that loaded material to make connections, plan, and recharge. A break taken before any deep loading has nothing to work with — the mind just drifts aimlessly. That is why insights arrive on the walk after the work session, and why the break is a functional stage rather than a mere reward.",
