     "type": "application",
     "title": "Build Your Rhythm Tomorrow",
     "content": "You do not need to overhaul your life — you need to run one clean cycle and let it repeat. Set this up for tomorrow.\n\n1. **Prime the day (5 min, scatterfocus).** Before opening any app, sit with a coffee and let your mind wander to one question: *what is the single most important thing to focus on today?* Write it down. This is your day's anchor.\n\n2. **Schedule two or three hyperfocus blocks.** Put 45-to-90-minute blocks on your calendar during your highest-energy windows. Before each: phone away, one task open, notifications off, distractions removed. Guard these like meetings you cannot cancel.\n\n3. **Follow every block with real scatterfocus.** After each focused block, take a 10-to-20-minute deliberate break — ideally a silent walk in nature, no screen. Let your loaded mind process. Keep a note handy to catch the insights that surface.\n\n4. **Batch shallow work into low-energy windows.** Cluster email, messages, and admin into one or two windows during energy troughs — never scatter them through your peak. Match energy to task.\n\n5. **Close with a capture-and-review (10 min).** At day's end, run a mind sweep to empty open loops, note what worked, and set tomorrow's anchor. This clears your space for real rest and primes the next cycle.\n\nThat is the whole system: prime, focus, wander, batch, recharge, review — then repeat. Bailey's promise is not that you will work more hours, but that the hours you work will be dramatically more productive and far more sustainable. Run one honest cycle tomorrow, notice the difference, and let the rhythm become the way you work.",
